  "family": "focus-and-replay",
  "description": "The story's end state: the promise token (●) in Party B's rack and the performance token (◆) in Party A's rack, joined by the plain line \"Linked as supplied\", and the strip \"Sequence as supplied (illustrative)\". A lens enlarges the link's station (a real copy of the scene, ≥ 1.5×); its label — the supplied status \"Performance identified (as supplied)\" — is struck, then turns over in the scene and returns with the supplied alternative \"Question to be analysed (as supplied)\"; only the link's dependent state follows (the dashed pending marker, an open question — not a failure). The lens closes onto the identical station; a Δ marks the changed label and the struck old value stays readable. The concept label \"consideration\" is shown as supplied and illustrative; no rule about it and no legal effect is stated.",
